g=a6?'- A meeting or appointment at a time is "event".':'- Never use "event": the person puts things on their calendar by starting with the word "calendar". A meeting or appointment at a time is a "task" with that date and time.'
f=o.length===0?"":" ("+o+")"
a2=i?"":'- "place" is, for a task tied to a place ("buy milk when I reach Shwapno", "call Ammu when I leave the office"), one of their saved places: '+B.b.aH(a2,", ")+'. "placeWhen" is "arrive" or "leave". Otherwise null. A task with a place needs no date.\n'
i=n?'- "remember": lasting facts about the person or their world that would help next time: who people are to them, their teams, places, preferences, routines, goals, what they study or own (like "Supports Manchester United", "Oishi is their sister", "Goes to the gym at 6 am on weekdays"). Short, third person, one fact each. Never one-off events, tasks, money amounts, moods, or passwords, ID or card numbers. If a fact above is repeated or confirmed by this note, return it again in the same words. Usually empty.\n':""
e=a9?' If it needs the internet, make "web" a full query that names the subject.':""
d=a9?'- "web": if answering needs the internet (news, weather, prices, scores, facts about the world, places, public people) and their data above does not answer it, a short search query for it, with no personal details from their data; then "reply" can be empty. Otherwise null. Never for their own plans, money, habits or notes.\n':""
